        "text": "Graphical Remoting Protocols\nConnecting remotely to the graphical user interface of both Windows and Linux\ncan be achieved easily these days. In this section, you will learn how to identify\na remoting protocol service and how to hack it like the pros. These are the most\ncommon applications that are used for this purpose:\nI\nI Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) : TCP port 3389\nI\nI Virtual Network Computing (VNC) : TCP port 5900\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 RDP (Port 3389)\n\u2022 VNC (Port 5900)\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
